# AICL Example: Computer Vision Pipeline
# Production computer vision pipeline covering image classification, object detection, semantic
# segmentation, face recognition, and video analysis with real-time and batch processing support.

Goal Build a comprehensive computer vision pipeline that provides image classification, object detection, segmentation, face recognition, and video analysis capabilities with real-time inference support and production-grade reliability

Constraint Image classification must achieve top-1 accuracy above 0.90 on ImageNet-scale benchmarks
Constraint Object detection must achieve mAP above 0.45 on COCO benchmark at 30+ FPS
Constraint Face recognition must maintain false positive rate below 0.001 at 99% true positive rate
Constraint Video analysis must process streams at minimum 30 FPS with frame-level inference
Constraint All biometric data must comply with GDPR and local privacy regulations with automatic deletion policies

Risk Model adversarial attack causing misclassification of manipulated images
Recovery Implement adversarial robustness training; deploy input perturbation detection; maintain ensemble of models for consensus-based classification

Risk Face recognition bias across demographic groups
Recovery Conduct regular fairness audits across skin tone and gender groups; enforce equalized odds constraints; deploy demographic-specific calibration

Risk GPU memory overflow during high-resolution image or video processing
Recovery Implement dynamic resolution scaling with tiling strategy; apply gradient checkpointing for training; enforce memory budget with graceful degradation to lower resolution

Risk Object detection failure in low-light or occluded conditions
Recovery Train on augmented data including low-light and occlusion scenarios; deploy multi-scale feature pyramid networks; use temporal aggregation for video frames

Risk Video stream processing lag causing frame drops during peak load
Recovery Implement frame sampling and priority queue; deploy adaptive quality reduction; maintain buffer with skip-frame fallback strategy

Risk Privacy violation from storing biometric face embeddings without consent
Recovery Implement automatic TTL-based deletion for face embeddings; enforce consent verification before storage; apply differential privacy to embedding vectors

Layer VisionCore
    SubLayer: ImagePreprocessing
    SubLayer: FeatureExtraction
    SubLayer: ModelInference
Layer VisionTasks
    SubLayer: Classification
    SubLayer: ObjectDetection
    SubLayer: Segmentation
    SubLayer: FaceRecognition
    SubLayer: VideoAnalysis
Layer VisionInfrastructure
    SubLayer: ModelServing
    SubLayer: GPUResourceManager
    SubLayer: StorageManager

Validation Image classification top-1 accuracy must exceed 0.90 on held-out test set
Validation Object detection mAP must exceed 0.45 on COCO-format evaluation
Validation Segmentation mIoU must exceed 0.65 on benchmark dataset
Validation Face recognition must achieve TAR above 0.99 at FAR below 0.001
Validation Video processing throughput must maintain 30 FPS minimum
Validation Adversarial robustness must pass FGSM and PGD attack benchmarks
Validation Face recognition fairness must show equalized odds difference below 0.1 across demographic groups
Validation GPU memory utilization must remain below 90% during peak inference load

# Level 2 - Entities

Entity ImageAsset
    imageId: string
    storageUri: string
    width: integer
    height: integer
    channels: integer
    format: string
    fileSizeBytes: integer
    captureTimestamp: datetime
    sourceDevice: string
    checksumHash: string
    metadata: dict

Entity DetectionResult
    resultId: string
    imageId: string
    detections: list
    boundingBoxes: list
    classLabels: list
    confidenceScores: list
    modelVersion: string
    inferenceTimeMs: float
    processedAt: datetime

Entity SegmentationMap
    mapId: string
    imageId: string
    segmentLabels: list
    segmentMasks: list
    segmentConfidences: list
    mIoUScore: float
    modelVersion: string
    processedAt: datetime

Entity FaceEmbedding
    embeddingId: string
    faceRegion: dict
    embeddingVector: list
    qualityScore: float
    demographicTags: dict
    consentStatus: boolean
    expirationTimestamp: datetime
    modelVersion: string
    createdAt: datetime

Entity VideoStream
    streamId: string
    sourceUri: string
    resolution: dict
    frameRate: float
    codec: string
    startTime: datetime
    endTime: datetime
    processingStatus: string
    frameBuffer: dict

Entity VisionModelConfig
    modelId: string
    taskType: string
    architecture: string
    inputResolution: dict
    batchSize: integer
    precision: string
    calibrationData: dict
    version: string
    performanceMetrics: dict

# Level 3 - Behaviors

Behavior ClassifyImage
    Input:
        image: ImageAsset
        modelConfig: VisionModelConfig
    Output:
        classification: dict
        confidence: float
    Action:
        Load and preprocess image to model input resolution
        Apply normalization using ImageNet statistics
        Run forward pass through classification model
        Apply softmax to obtain class probabilities
        Return top-K predictions with confidence scores

Behavior DetectObjects
    Input:
        image: ImageAsset
        modelConfig: VisionModelConfig
        confidenceThreshold: float
    Output:
        detectionResult: DetectionResult
    Action:
        Preprocess image with letterbox resizing
        Run object detection model forward pass
        Apply non-maximum suppression to filter overlapping boxes
        Filter detections by confidence threshold
        Map class indices to human-readable labels
        Return all detections with bounding boxes and scores

Behavior SegmentImage
    Input:
        image: ImageAsset
        modelConfig: VisionModelConfig
    Output:
        segmentationMap: SegmentationMap
    Action:
        Preprocess image and run through segmentation model
        Resize output logits to original image dimensions
        Apply argmax to obtain per-pixel class predictions
        Generate instance masks for each segment
        Compute mIoU if ground truth is available
        Return segmentation map with all labels and masks

Behavior RecognizeFace
    Input:
        image: ImageAsset
        faceRegion: dict
        modelConfig: VisionModelConfig
    Output:
        faceEmbedding: FaceEmbedding
        matchResult: dict
    Action:
        Align face using detected landmarks
        Crop and normalize face region to model input size
        Compute face embedding vector
        Search embedding against gallery for matches
        Apply distance threshold for identity verification
        Check consent status before storing or returning match
        Return embedding and match result with confidence

Behavior AnalyzeVideoStream
    Input:
        videoStream: VideoStream
        analysisConfig: dict
    Output:
        frameResults: list
        streamSummary: dict
    Action:
        Initialize frame buffer and sampling strategy
        Process frames at target FPS through appropriate models
        Aggregate temporal information across frames
        Track objects across frames using optical flow
        Generate stream-level summary with key events
        Return frame-by-frame results and stream summary

Behavior PreprocessImage
    Input:
        image: ImageAsset
        preprocessingConfig: dict
    Output:
        processedImage: ImageAsset
        preprocessingReport: dict
    Action:
        Decode image from storage format
        Apply EXIF orientation correction
        Resize to target dimensions maintaining aspect ratio
        Apply color space normalization
        Detect and handle corrupted pixel regions
        Return preprocessed image ready for inference

# Level 4 - Conditions

Condition: AdversarialInputSuspected
    When input perturbation detection score exceeds threshold
    Then flag image for manual review; run ensemble models for consensus; log adversarial detection event with image metadata

Condition: FaceQualityBelowThreshold
    When face quality score falls below 0.6 due to blur, occlusion, or angle
    Then reject face recognition attempt; return quality failure reason; log low-quality face detection for model improvement

Condition: GPUMemoryPressure
    When GPU memory utilization exceeds 85% during inference
    Then reduce batch size dynamically; enable model offloading to CPU; queue excess requests with priority scheduling

Condition: VideoFrameDropDetected
    When frame processing latency exceeds frame interval causing dropped frames
    Then activate frame skip strategy; reduce analysis resolution; alert monitoring system of throughput degradation

Condition: BiometricConsentMissing
    When face embedding is requested for storage but consent status is false
    Then discard embedding immediately; return privacy-compliant response; log consent violation attempt for audit

# Level 5 - Events

Event: ImageSubmitted
    On new image received for processing
    Action: validate image format and integrity; enqueue for preprocessing; log submission metadata

Event: DetectionCompleted
    On object detection inference completed
    Action: publish results to downstream consumers; update detection statistics; cache results for similar images

Event: FaceMatchFound
    On face recognition returning identity match above threshold
    Action: verify consent for identity disclosure; log match with audit trail; notify access control system if required

Event: VideoStreamStarted
    On video stream connected and frame processing initiated
    Action: initialize frame buffer; allocate GPU resources; start temporal tracking; emit stream health metrics

Event: AdversarialAlert
    On adversarial input detected by robustness module
    Action: quarantine image for review; alert security team; update adversarial example database; block similar inputs

Event: ModelPerformanceDegraded
    On inference metrics falling below SLA thresholds
    Action: trigger model health check; activate fallback model; alert on-call engineer; initiate performance investigation

# Level 6 - Concurrency

Parallel:
    Image preprocessing across multiple input images simultaneously
    Classification, detection, and segmentation inference on different GPU streams
    Face alignment and embedding computation concurrently
    Video frame decoding and inference pipeline overlap
    Model serving across multiple GPU devices
    Feature extraction backbone shared across task heads concurrently

# Level 7 - Optimization

Optimize: Inference throughput and latency
    Priority: Maximize FPS for object detection; use TensorRT optimization and INT8 quantization; batch similar-sized images

Optimize: GPU memory utilization
    Priority: Dynamic batching with padding optimization; model weight sharing across tasks; gradient checkpointing during training

Optimize: Video stream processing efficiency
    Priority: Adaptive frame sampling based on scene change detection; temporal model reuse for static scenes; priority-based frame scheduling

# Level 8 - Learning

Learn: Optimal preprocessing parameters per image domain
    Goal: Maximize downstream task accuracy through adaptive preprocessing
    Adapt: Normalization parameters, resize strategy, augmentation pipeline
    Based: Task-specific performance metrics across different image domains

Learn: Face recognition threshold calibration
    Goal: Equalize false positive and false negative rates across demographic groups
    Adapt: Distance thresholds and quality score cutoffs per demographic segment
    Based: Fairness audit results and cross-demographic matching performance data

Learn: Video frame sampling strategy
    Goal: Process minimum frames while maintaining detection quality
    Adapt: Sampling rate, scene change sensitivity, keyframe selection criteria
    Based: Comparison of full-frame vs sampled analysis quality metrics

Learn: Adversarial robustness through attack simulation
    Goal: Improve model resilience against adversarial perturbations
    Adapt: Model weights through adversarial training with projected gradient descent
    Based: Performance on generated adversarial examples and robustness benchmarks

# Level 9 - Security

Security:
    Encrypt: Face embedding vectors at rest using AES-256 with per-tenant key management
    Encrypt: All image data in transit with TLS 1.3 and certificate pinning
    Protect: Biometric data with automatic TTL expiration and consent-gated access
    Protect: Model weights with signed artifact verification before loading
    Protect: Video stream access with IP allowlisting and token-based authentication
    Encrypt: Detection results containing sensitive content with field-level encryption
    Protect: Adversarial detection logs from tampering via append-only audit trail

# Level 10 - Native

Native: python
{
import numpy as np
from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple
from dataclasses import dataclass, field
from datetime import datetime, timedelta

@dataclass
class ImagePreprocessor:
    target_size: Tuple[int, int] = (224, 224)
    normalize_mean: List[float] = field(default_factory=lambda: [0.485, 0.456, 0.406])
    normalize_std: List[float] = field(default_factory=lambda: [0.229, 0.224, 0.225])
    max_pixel_value: float = 255.0

    def preprocess(self, image: np.ndarray, maintain_aspect: bool = True) -> np.ndarray:
        if maintain_aspect:
            h, w = image.shape[:2]
            scale = min(self.target_size[0] / h, self.target_size[1] / w)
            new_h, new_w = int(h * scale), int(w * scale)
            image = self._resize(image, new_h, new_w)
            image = self._pad_to_size(image, self.target_size)
        else:
            image = self._resize(image, self.target_size[0], self.target_size[1])

        image = image.astype(np.float32) / self.max_pixel_value
        image = (image - np.array(self.normalize_mean)) / np.array(self.normalize_std)
        image = np.transpose(image, (2, 0, 1))
        return image

    def _resize(self, image: np.ndarray, h: int, w: int) -> np.ndarray:
        from PIL import Image
        pil_image = Image.fromarray(image)
        pil_image = pil_image.resize((w, h), Image.BILINEAR)
        return np.array(pil_image)

    def _pad_to_size(self, image: np.ndarray, target_size: Tuple[int, int]) -> np.ndarray:
        h, w = image.shape[:2]
        pad_h = max(0, target_size[0] - h)
        pad_w = max(0, target_size[1] - w)
        if pad_h > 0 or pad_w > 0:
            image = np.pad(image, ((0, pad_h), (0, pad_w), (0, 0)), mode='constant')
        return image[:target_size[0], :target_size[1]]

@dataclass
class FaceQualityAssessor:
    min_resolution: int = 80
    max_yaw: float = 30.0
    max_pitch: float = 30.0
    min_sharpness: float = 0.3

    def assess(self, face_crop: np.ndarray, landmarks: Dict) -> Dict:
        h, w = face_crop.shape[:2]
        resolution_score = min(1.0, min(h, w) / self.min_resolution)
        sharpness = self._compute_sharpness(face_crop)
        sharpness_score = min(1.0, sharpness / self.min_sharpness) if self.min_sharpness > 0 else 1.0
        pose_scores = self._estimate_pose(landmarks)
        overall = (resolution_score * 0.3 + sharpness_score * 0.3 +
                   pose_scores["yaw_score"] * 0.2 + pose_scores["pitch_score"] * 0.2)
        return {
            "overall_quality": overall,
            "resolution_score": resolution_score,
            "sharpness_score": sharpness_score,
            "pose_scores": pose_scores,
            "passes_threshold": overall >= 0.6
        }

    def _compute_sharpness(self, image: np.ndarray) -> float:
        gray = np.mean(image, axis=2) if len(image.shape) == 3 else image
        laplacian_var = np.var(np.array([[0, -1, 0], [-1, 4, -1], [0, -1, 0]]))
        return float(laplacian_var)

    def _estimate_pose(self, landmarks: Dict) -> Dict:
        yaw_score = 1.0 - min(1.0, abs(landmarks.get("yaw", 0)) / self.max_yaw)
        pitch_score = 1.0 - min(1.0, abs(landmarks.get("pitch", 0)) / self.max_pitch)
        return {"yaw_score": yaw_score, "pitch_score": pitch_score}

@dataclass
class FrameSampler:
    target_fps: float = 30.0
    scene_change_threshold: float = 0.3
    max_skip_frames: int = 5

    def should_process_frame(self, current_frame: np.ndarray,
                             previous_frame: Optional[np.ndarray],
                             frame_count: int) -> bool:
        if frame_count == 0:
            return True
        if previous_frame is None:
            return True
        diff = np.mean(np.abs(
            current_frame.astype(float) - previous_frame.astype(float)
        )) / 255.0
        if diff > self.scene_change_threshold:
            return True
        skip_interval = max(1, int(30.0 / self.target_fps))
        return frame_count % skip_interval == 0
}
